abstract: >-
  A simulation model of how a science funder should allocate grants across
  researchers and over T funding rounds to maximize scientific output, comparing
  naive, myopic-Bayesian, and forward-looking (certainty-equivalent) planners.
  Researchers differ in latent knowledge and resources; output is bottlenecked by
  the scarcer input and knowledge compounds between rounds. Includes the model
  engine, an interactive Shiny explorer, the full parameter-sweep dataset, and a
  validation/reproducibility suite.
